// THE TRADING TAX ON THE ZANARIS MARKET GATE, and the four Gate Keepers who collect it.
//
// The market is the walled compound in the south-east of Zanaris that holds Irksol, Jukat's dragon
// sword stall and the rest of the stalls. Two magic doors lead into it and four Gate Keepers -
// mindslayers, and all brothers - stand two to a door. Every one of them offered Talk-to with
// nothing behind it, and the doors opened for free.
//
// They did not open for free in 2006. The doors (cache ids 12045-12048) and the Gate Keepers both
// arrived on 27 February 2006 with A Fairy Tale Part I, and the npc is still called "Gate Keeper"
// here - it was renamed to "Gatekeeper" on 5 December 2006 - so this build sits inside the window
// where the tax was one cut diamond. Dialogue verbatim from
// oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Transcript:Gatekeeper.
//
// WHICH SIDE IS WHICH, measured rather than assumed. A walkability flood with both gates shut
// splits Zanaris in two and the two halves never touch: 3,313 tiles holding the fairy ring, the
// wheat field and the bank, and a 1,069-tile compound holding Irksol. The compound is SOUTH of the
// south gate (two doors at z 4434, angle 3 - a wall on the south edge of their own tiles) and EAST
// of the east gate (two doors at x 2469, angle 2 - a wall on the east edge of their own tiles). So
// in both gates the door's own tile is on the OUTSIDE, which is what ~zanaris_market_gate_inside
// leans on. Leaving is free; nobody pays to get out of a market.
//
// This is a deliberate re-gating of content that was opened on purpose. The doors had no category
// and no script at all and the market was unreachable - "zanaris - cant enter area to buy dragon
// long and dds" - so configs/zanaris_gate.loc handed them to the double-door framework. That fixed
// the wrong half: the gate was painted shut, and the fix painted it open. A diamond is the right
// answer. If it ever needs to be free again, delete the two [oploc1] triggers below and the
// category handlers in doors/scripts/doubledoors.rs2 take the doors straight back.
//
// THERE IS A SECOND DIAMOND TAX IN THIS REPOSITORY AND IT IS DEAD. doorman.rs2 answers
// [oploc1,zanarismarketdoor] with the same conversation in its RuneScape Classic wording, and
// zanarismarketdoor (loc 2411) is placed on no map square in this build - the coords it hunts the
// Door man at, 0_50_149_35_22, are x 3235 z 9558, nowhere near Zanaris. It is the older door and
// the older npc, kept rather than deleted. The live gate is the one below. If the two ever
// disagree, this is the one a player can reach.
//
// NOT IMPLEMENTED, and noted so the next reader does not think it was missed: the transcript's
// "Sorry, we cannot allow you to bring those sacks into the market for security reasons." There is
// no evidence for when that rule arrived and sack_empty is an ordinary 377 obj with no quest
// attached, so refusing entry over one would be inventing a restriction.

[oploc1,fairy_mushroom_gate_door_l]
if (~zanaris_market_gate_let_through = false) {
    return;
}
~open_double_doors_left(500, door_right_closed, loc_param(open_sound));

[oploc1,fairy_mushroom_gate_door_r]
if (~zanaris_market_gate_let_through = false) {
    return;
}
~open_double_doors_right(500, door_left_closed, loc_param(open_sound));

[proc,zanaris_market_gate_let_through]()(boolean)
if (~zanaris_market_gate_inside = true) {
    return(true);
}
~zanaris_gatekeeper_says("<p,neutral>You may not pass through this door without paying the trading tax.");
~chatplayer("<p,quiz>So how much is the tax?");
~zanaris_gatekeeper_says("<p,neutral>The cost is one diamond.");
switch_int(~p_choice4("Okay...", 1, "A diamond? Are you crazy?", 2, "I haven't brought my diamonds with me.", 3, "What do you do with all the diamonds you get?", 4)) {
    case 1 :
        ~chatplayer("<p,neutral>Okay...");
        if (inv_total(inv, diamond) < 1) {
            ~chatplayer("<p,sad>...but...");
            ~chatplayer("<p,sad>I haven't brought my diamonds with me.");
            ~zanaris_gatekeeper_says("<p,neutral>No tax, no entry.");
            return(false);
        }
        inv_del(inv, diamond, 1);
        if_close;
        // "doorman", not "Gate Keeper". The line is the game's own and it has said doorman since
        // the old man had the job - which is what the Gate Keeper's own Talk-to is about.
        mes("You give the doorman a diamond.");
        return(true);
    case 2 :
        ~chatplayer("<p,confused>A diamond?|Are you crazy?");
        ~zanaris_gatekeeper_says("<p,neutral>Not at all. Those are the rules.");
    case 3 :
        ~chatplayer("<p,sad>I haven't brought my diamonds with me.");
        ~zanaris_gatekeeper_says("<p,neutral>No tax, no entry.");
    case 4 :
        ~chatplayer("<p,quiz>What do you do with all the diamonds you get?");
        ~zanaris_gatekeeper_says("<p,happy>Ever heard of fairylights? Well how do you think we make 'em? First we collect a pile of gems and then we get a spider to spin 'em into a long web, we light the jewels by imbuing each one with a little bit of magic.");
        ~chatplayer("<p,shock>So you're telling me fairylights are made out of gems?");
        ~zanaris_gatekeeper_says("<p,happy>That's right, how else could we make 'em twinkle so beautifully?");
}
return(false);

// Is the player already in the market, i.e. on the far side of the wall from the door's own tile?
// The wall sits on the loc tile's loc_angle edge, so the tile across that edge is the inside one.
// Written for all four angles rather than only the two these gates use, because a loc that is
// rotated in the map data later should not silently start charging players on the way out.
[proc,zanaris_market_gate_inside]()(boolean)
switch_int(loc_angle) {
    case ^loc_south :
        if (coordz(coord) < coordz(loc_coord)) {
            return(true);
        }
    case ^loc_north :
        if (coordz(coord) > coordz(loc_coord)) {
            return(true);
        }
    case ^loc_east :
        if (coordx(coord) > coordx(loc_coord)) {
            return(true);
        }
    case ^loc_west :
        if (coordx(coord) < coordx(loc_coord)) {
            return(true);
        }
}
return(false);

// The Gate Keeper's own Talk-to, which is about the job rather than the tax: he has inherited it
// from the old man who used to stand here, and is pleased not to look like him.
[opnpc1,fairy_mindslayer]
~chatplayer("<p,quiz>What happened to the old man who used to be the doorman?");
~chatnpc("<p,neutral>You mean my father? He went into retirement, I've taken over the family business instead.");
~chatplayer("<p,shock>Your father! But you don't look anything like him!");
~chatnpc("<p,happy>No, fortunately for me I inherited my good looks from my mother.");

// Said by a Gate Keeper when the player clicked a door rather than the npc, so there is no active
// npc to speak as. nc_name rather than a literal, because this build still spells it "Gate Keeper".
[proc,zanaris_gatekeeper_says](string $line)
~chatnpc_specific(nc_name(fairy_mindslayer), fairy_mindslayer, $line);
